Error [jet.SecretAtBuildTime]: `core.crypto.vault.get()` can't be reached from a build-time context
  --> tests/ui/secret_in_build.jet:4:27
    |
  4 |     cfg: comptime { vault.get("db_password") }
    |                           ^^^
 Why: Module-field and comptime evaluation run before secrets are decrypted. A repository opens its encrypted store only at ordinary runtime, such as inside a `-[Secret]>` function. There is no audited gate escape because a build artifact must never contain a decrypted secret.
 Fix: Move the secret read out of comptime or module-field evaluation and into ordinary runtime code.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E1265
